  "see_also": [],
  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "Many languages say the one I like most with a superlative; English uses this ordinary adjective before the noun, almost always with a possessive: my favorite, her favorite.",
    "grammar": "Favorite comes before a noun (my favorite song) or stands as a noun (this is my favorite); it is not used after be as an adjective, and it takes no most or very.",
    "culture": null,
    "false_friends": null,
    "pronunciation": "Often said with two syllables, fave-rit, with the middle vowel dropped; the full three-syllable form is also correct. The stress is on the first syllable."
  },
